 "final_message": "I applied with Brightpath Home Lending (application BHL-26001), answered the underwriting condition, and recorded Sam and Nadia's intent to proceed on the Loan Estimate.\n\n- **Lender choice:** Brightpath had the lowest 30-year fixed rate that fits the limits, 6.25%. Cascade's 6.125% option has $19,450 in closing costs, and its no-points option is 6.625%, above the 6.5% cap. Summit Ridge was 6.375%.\n- **Application:** I filled in and submitted it once, with the credit-check, e-sign and certification boxes checked. I uploaded only the last two statements (August and September) for each of the four authorized accounts, plus the last two payslips for each of them. I left out Nadia's business checking account.\n- **Underwriting condition:** The lender asked about an $8,000 deposit on 09/03 into Sam's checking. Sam and Nadia told me it was a gift from Sam's parents toward the down payment, not a loan. I sent that explanation. The page shows \"response received\", but the application status still read \"Loan Estimate issued; conditional review\" when I last looked.\n- **Loan Estimate:** The rate is 6.25%, the monthly payment is $3,042.41 and closing costs are $12,850. All three are within their limits (6.5%, $3,100 and $14,000), so I submitted the intent to proceed. Brightpath confirmed it with an \"Intent to proceed received\" page.\n\nThe estimate's cash to close is $122,850 and it comes with a 45-day rate lock option.",
